        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I'm not really sure whether `auto` can simplify anything here, or whether it would help with the resize code. The duplicated code you mentioned is mostly the calculation of `row, col, height, width, and anchor`. These calculations are needed in different scenarios, so some amount of code duplication is unavoidable. The same applies to the resize PR, most of the logic is about calculating the window position. `ui_ext_win_position`  contains some fallback logic, such as window from going out of bounds.\r\n\r\nVim's popup positioning logic is also quite complicated. This implementation simplifies some of Vim's odd behaviors, such as the pum being positioned above the cursor in certain cases.",
